    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive outlook, anchored by **Junior Caminero** (78.72) and **Yordan Alvarez** (75.77). **Junior Caminero** occupies the top spot in our lineup efficiency today, capitalizing on a favorable matchup against Grayson Rodriguez, whose 4.74 xERA provides a significant cushion for power production. Similarly, **Yordan Alvarez** remains an auto-start; his elite xwOBA of .452 combined with a +7% platoon advantage against Kolek creates the highest ceiling on the roster. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (62.50) serves as our most important catalyst; despite facing a high-skill arm in Logan Webb, his leadoff placement and +14% dynamic platoon advantage leverage his elite sprint speed to keep the Zebras competitive in the scarce SB category.\n\nOur rotation decisions were guided by strict adherence to the 40.0 floor, which ultimately left **Chase Meidroth** (36.97) on the bench. While **Chase Meidroth** offered moderate utility, his exposure to Gavin Sheehan\u2019s 3.38 xERA suppressed his floor, making him a liability compared to the higher-upside profiles of **Carson Benge** or **Lars Nootbaar**. We continue to monitor the status of **Colt Keith**, whose game has been flagged as a rainout, and we remain cautious regarding **Gary Sanchez**, who is priced down to 43.23 today due to a brutal matchup against Cristopher S\u00e1nchez (2.72 xERA). Managers should note that while **Kyle Schwarber** (56.05) and **Trea Turner** (55.76) face a tough challenge in the form of Harrison\u2019s 3.39 xERA, their positional value and order seniority keep them well above our threshold. We are holding tight with the rest of the prospect depth, including **Hyeseong Kim** and **Rece Hinds**, as they remain sidelined in the minors waiting for a path to active duty.",
